! vfl_lft_decimal.strap -- decimal LOAD FACTOR, built 2026-11-16 (G2.3,
! the last decimal VFL refusal).  Reference Manual printed p.69 (PDF 72),
! read in the page image:
!
!   "The factor register (FT) is cleared.  A four-bit sign byte, in which
!   the leftmost bit is the sign of the addressed storage operand as
!   modified by the negative sign modifier, is placed in the four
!   low-order bits of FT.  The remaining three bits of this sign byte are
!   zero.  The numeric part of the addressed operand is positioned to the
!   left of this sign byte in FT."
!   MODIFIERS: "Unsigned; Negative Sign; Radix.  These modifiers operate
!   as in ADD."
!   PF: "Since the four low-order bits of FT are used as a sign byte,
!   only 60 numeric bits can be loaded into FT.  This indicator is turned
!   on if the numeric part of the field loaded contains more than 60
!   significant bits.  If this occurs, FT is loaded up to its left end.
!   Higher-order bits are lost."
!   Arithmetic result: "set according to the contents of the factor
!   register when the operation is complete."
!
! "Radix ... as in ADD" is printed p.60's and p.58's: in decimal "each
! byte of the storage operand is converted to a four-bit byte ... by the
! addition of high-order zeros" -- so the numeric part that goes into FT
! is four-bit digits, whatever the byte size; sixty bits is fifteen of
! them.  HAND-DERIVED cases, no IBM oracle exists for this one:
!
!   L1 LFT(DU,24,4) of 123456: FT = (16)1234560, RGZ.
!   L2 LFT(DU,18,6) of three six-bit bytes with zones 11 (110001 110010
!      110011, as decks/vfl_decimal_add.strap's Z123): the zones are
!      dropped, FT = (16)1230.  A binary LFT of the same field would
!      load (16)31CB3 shifted -- this is the case that tells the radices
!      apart.
!   L3 LFT(DU,64,4) of sixteen digits 1234567890123456: sixteen digits
!      are 64 bits, more than 60, PF; FT keeps the low fifteen,
!      (16)2345678901234560.
!   L4 LFT(D,16,4) of 000- (three zero digits, sign byte 1000): FT =
!      (16)8 -- the sign bit at FT bit 60 and a zero numeric part -- and
!      RZ with RN ("negative whether zero or not", printed p.47).
!   L5 LFTN(DU,8,4) of 42: unsigned is positive, the negative sign
!      modifier inverts it: FT = (16)428, RLZ and RN.
! Each clears the indicators first and copies FT and the indicators out.
!
! INJECTIONS, measured: tests/run_tests.sh, this deck's line.

        SLC, 1000.0
START   Z, $IND
        LFT(DU,24,4), L1D
        TI, 1, $FT, L1FT
        TI, 1, $IND, L1IND
        Z, $IND
        LFT(DU,18,6), L2D
        TI, 1, $FT, L2FT
        TI, 1, $IND, L2IND
        Z, $IND
        LFT(DU,64,4), L3D
        TI, 1, $FT, L3FT
        TI, 1, $IND, L3IND
        Z, $IND
        LFT(D,16,4), L4D
        TI, 1, $FT, L4FT
        TI, 1, $IND, L4IND
        Z, $IND
        LFTN(DU,8,4), L5D
        TI, 1, $FT, L5FT
        TI, 1, $IND, L5IND
HALT    BEW, $

        SLC, 1100.0
L1D     DD(BU,64), (16)1234560000000000
L2D     DD(BU,64), (16)C72CC00000000000
L3D     DD(BU,64), (16)1234567890123456
L4D     DD(BU,64), (16)0008000000000000
L5D     DD(BU,64), (16)4200000000000000

        SLC, 1200.0
L1FT    DD(BU,64), 0
L2FT    DD(BU,64), 0
L3FT    DD(BU,64), 0
L4FT    DD(BU,64), 0
L5FT    DD(BU,64), 0
L1IND   DD(BU,64), 0
L2IND   DD(BU,64), 0
L3IND   DD(BU,64), 0
L4IND   DD(BU,64), 0
L5IND   DD(BU,64), 0

        END, START
